{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-robustness","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"New bash fallback paths, sentinel logic, and FD-3 routing introduce bash-3.2-compat risks and pipefail interaction edge cases not covered by generic correctness reviewers.","prompt_body":"Audit the new shell code in `scripts/render-run-summary.sh`, `skills/implement/scripts/write-final-report.sh`, and `skills/design/scripts/render-final-summary.sh` for bash 3.2 compatibility (array append `+=`, `[[ ]]` constructs, `mapfile`, etc.). Check that `set -euo pipefail` is handled correctly around the new `set +e`/`set -e` fallback blocks — verify exit codes are captured before `set -e` is restored, and that `render_or_fallback`'s `allow_fallback` branching can't silently swallow the wrong return code. Verify that the new `LARCH_QUIET_PID` FD-3 chat-print loop in `render-final-summary.sh` correctly falls back to FD 1 when `LARCH_QUIET_PID` is unset (not just `!= $$`), and that `lib-quiet.sh` is sourced before `larch_quiet_init` is called in all code paths. Check whether `PLUGIN_ROOT` vs `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` usage is consistent across the modified scripts. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-fixture-gaps","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"The outcome-matrix loop in test-write-final-report.sh references variables like $impl_dir, $impl_st, $impl_do, $impl_bu that are not defined within the diff, and make_impl_fixture may not create run-flags.sh needed by write-final-report.sh.","prompt_body":"Examine `skills/implement/scripts/test-write-final-report.sh` for the outcome-matrix loop that iterates over `merged`, `stalled`, `design-only`, etc. Check whether the fixture variables `$impl_dir`, `$impl_st`, `$impl_do`, `$impl_bu` referenced in the loop body are defined earlier in the file (either in the diff context or as pre-existing test setup). Verify that the `make_impl_fixture` helper creates all files `write-final-report.sh` requires (`run-flags.sh`, correct `finalize-state.sh` fields like `BAIL_NEEDS_USER_INPUT` and `DESIGN_ONLY_DONE`). Also check `skills/design/scripts/test-render-final-summary.sh` for the ten-outcome matrix loop: confirm each outcome passes an `approved-partition` / `approved` without an Outcome bullet correctly, and that the `PLUGIN_STUB` is still set up with `lib-quiet.sh` for the matrix iterations that reuse it after the renderer-fail block that restores `render-run-summary.sh`. Identify any test cases that would silently pass due to missing fixtures or unset variables. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"skill-prose-consistency","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"SKILL.md Step 17 sentinel write is conditioned on both script success AND cost-line presence, while the plan describes only script success; the test and callsite lint check different conditions, risking a mismatch.","prompt_body":"Read the Step 17 Bash block in `skills/implement/SKILL.md` (the `if` that wraps `write-final-report.sh --print-stdout` and the `touch .step17-printed` sentinel). Verify that the sentinel write condition exactly matches what `test-render-cost-line-callsites.sh` asserts: the callsite lint checks for the literal `write-final-report.sh\" --implement-tmpdir \"$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR\" --print-stdout; then` pattern and separately for `if [ \"$_wfr_printed\" = true ] && grep -Fq -- '- **Cost**:'` — confirm that both grep patterns will actually match the text present in SKILL.md, not just the intent. Check the Step 18 Bash block (`_wfr_args`, `_wfr_printed`, conditional cost-line emit prose) for internal consistency: if `write-final-report.sh` succeeds but `summary-final.md` contains no `- **Cost**:` line (Stage 2 self-compose failure), is the orchestrator prose correct about whether to emit the cost line? Also check whether the design SKILL.md anti-halt paragraph and the new NEVER rule at end of Step 5d are consistent — one says 'the only orchestrator-text addition permitted... is the single extracted `- **Cost**:` line' while the other says 'emit only warning repeats and the machine footer' — verify these are not contradictory for the Step 5c happy path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
